epts/resources#updatectx-prior-planned","content":"Called during `terraform apply` for in-place updates. `prior` is the current state; `planned` is what the user wants. Return the resulting state."},"270":{"id":"/docs/concepts/resources-22","page_id":"/docs/concepts/resources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/resources#deletectx-current","content":"Called during `terraform destroy`. No return value."},"271":{"id":"/docs/concepts/resources-23","page_id":"/docs/concepts/resources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/resources#validatediags-typename-config","content":"Custom validation during `terraform validate` / `terraform plan`. Called before `create` or `update`. Use this for cross-attribute validation that the schema can't express (e.g. \"if `region` is `us-east-1` then `zone` must be set\")."},"272":{"id":"/docs/concepts/resources-24","page_id":"/docs/concepts/resources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/resources#planctx-prior-planned","content":"Override the default plan behaviour. Useful for marking attributes as `Unknown` (known after apply) before you know what the API will return."},"273":{"id":"/docs/concepts/resources-25","page_id":"/docs/concepts/resources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/resources#importctx-id","content":"Support `terraform import`. Parse the `id` string and return the current state from the API, or `null` if the resource doesn't exist."},"274":{"id":"/docs/concepts/resources-26","page_id":"/docs/concepts/resources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/resources#importctx-id","content":"After importing, Terraform records the returned state and generates a plan to reconcile any differences with the config."},"275":{"id":"/docs/concepts/resources-27","page_id":"/docs/concepts/resources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/resources#upgradectx-version-old","content":"Migrate state when the schema `version` changes. See Schema migration for full patterns."},"276":{"id":"/docs/concepts/resources-28","page_id":"/docs/concepts/resources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/resources#context-objects","content":"Every lifecycle method receives a context as its first argument."},"277":{"id":"/docs/concepts/resources-29","page_id":"/docs/concepts/resources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/resources#context-objects","content":"`changedFields` uses **semantic equality** per field type. For example, a `types.normalizedJson()` attribute whose key order changed (but whose value is otherwise identical) will **not** appear in `changedFields`. A `\"set\"` nested block whose items are reordered will also **not** appear. This means you can safely use `changedFields` to decide whether to call a specific API endpoint, without false positives from cosmetic differences."},"278":{"id":"/docs/concepts/resources-30","page_id":"/docs/concepts/resources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/resources#datasource-interface","content":"Data sources are read-only. They have no create/update/delete — only `read`."},"279":{"id":"/docs/concepts/resources-31","page_id":"/docs/concepts/resources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/resources#datasource-interface","content":"**Example:**"},"280":{"id":"/docs/concepts/schema","page_id":"/docs/concepts/schema","type":"page","content":"Types & Schema","breadcrumbs":["terrably","Core concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/schema"},"281":{"id":"/docs/concepts/schema-0","page_id":"/docs/concepts/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/schema","content":"The TfType system, Attribute, Block, NestedBlock, and Schema — terrably's building blocks for describing provider resources."},"282":{"id":"/docs/concepts/schema-1","page_id":"/docs/concepts/schema","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/schema#types","content":"Types"},"283":{"id":"/docs/concepts/schema-2","page_id":"/docs/concepts/schema","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/schema#custom-tftypet","content":"Custom `TfType<T>`"},"284":{"id":"/docs/concepts/schema-3","page_id":"/docs/concepts/schema","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/schema#attribute","content":"Attribute"},"285":{"id":"/docs/concepts/schema-4","page_id":"/docs/concepts/schema","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/schema#attributeoptions","content":"`AttributeOptions`"},"286":{"id":"/docs/concepts/schema-5","page_id":"/docs/concepts/schema","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/schema#nestedblock","content":"NestedBlock"},"287":{"id":"/docs/concepts/schema-6","page_id":"/docs/concepts/schema","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/schema#blockoptions","content":"`BlockOptions`"},"288":{"id":"/docs/concepts/schema-7","page_id":"/docs/concepts/schema","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/schema#schema","content":"Schema"},"289":{"id":"/docs/concepts/schema-8","page_id":"/docs/concepts/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/schema#types","content":"Every attribute in a schema requires a `TfType`. Types are created via the `types` factory — each call returns a fresh instance."},"290":{"id":"/docs/concepts/schema-9","page_id":"/docs/concepts/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/schema#types","content":"<TypeTable\n  type=\"{\n  &#x22;types.string()&#x22;: {\n    description: &#x22;Terraform `string`. TypeScript: `string`.&#x22;,\n    type: &#x22;TfType<string>&#x22;,\n  },\n  &#x22;types.number()&#x22;: {\n    description: &#x22;Terraform `number`. TypeScript: `number`.&#x22;,\n    type: &#x22;TfType<number>&#x22;,\n  },\n  &#x22;types.bool()&#x22;: {\n    description: &#x22;Terraform `bool`. TypeScript: `boolean`.&#x22;,\n    type: &#x22;TfType<boolean>&#x22;,\n  },\n  &#x22;types.normalizedJson()&#x22;: {\n    description: &#x22;Terraform `string` (JSON round-tripped with sorted keys). TypeScript: `unknown`. Prevents spurious diffs from key reordering.&#x22;,\n    type: &#x22;TfType<unknown>&#x22;,\n  },\n  &#x22;types.list(T)&#x22;: {\n    description: &#x22;Terraform `list(T)`. TypeScript: `T[]`.&#x22;,\n    type: &#x22;TfType<T[]>&#x22;,\n  },\n  &#x22;types.set(T)&#x22;: {\n    description: &#x22;Terraform `set(T)`. TypeScript: `T[]`.&#x22;,\n    type: &#x22;TfType<T[]>&#x22;,\n  },\n  &#x22;types.map(T)&#x22;: {\n    description: &#x22;Terraform `map(T)`. TypeScript: `Record<string, T>`.&#x22;,\n    type: &#x22;TfType<Record<string, T>>&#x22;,\n  },\n}\"\n/>"},"291":{"id":"/docs/concepts/schema-10","page_id":"/docs/concepts/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/schema#types","content":"**Composing types**"},"292":{"id":"/docs/concepts/schema-11","page_id":"/docs/concepts/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/schema#custom-tftypet","content":"Implement this interface to define a custom type –"},"293":{"id":"/docs/concepts/schema-12","page_id":"/docs/concepts/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/schema#attribute","content":"Describes a single field in a resource or provider schema."},"294":{"id":"/docs/concepts/schema-13","page_id":"/docs/concepts/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/schema#attributeoptions","content":"<TypeTable\n  type=\"{\n  required: {\n    description: &#x22;User must provide this attribute in their config.&#x22;,\n    type: &#x22;boolean&#x22;,\n    default: &#x22;false&#x22;,\n  },\n  optional: {\n    description: &#x22;User may provide this attribute.&#x22;,\n    type: &#x22;boolean&#x22;,\n    default: &#x22;false&#x22;,\n  },\n  computed: {\n    description: &#x22;Provider computes this value. Cannot be set by the user unless also `optional`.&#x22;,\n    type: &#x22;boolean&#x22;,\n    default: &#x22;false&#x22;,\n  },\n  sensitive: {\n    description: &#x22;Value is redacted in plan output and stored encrypted in state. See [sensitive data in state](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/state/sensitive-data).&#x22;,\n    type: &#x22;boolean&#x22;,\n    default: &#x22;false&#x22;,\n  },\n  requiresReplace: {\n    description: &#x22;Changing this attribute [destroys and recreates the resource](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/plugin/framework/resources/plan-modification#requiresreplace).&#x22;,\n    type: &#x22;boolean&#x22;,\n    default: &#x22;false&#x22;,\n  },\n  description: {\n    description: &#x22;Shown in `terraform providers schema`.&#x22;,\n    type: &#x22;string&#x22;,\n    default: '&#x22;&#x22;',\n  },\n  descriptionKind: {\n    description: &#x22;Format of the description.&#x22;,\n    type: '&#x22;plain&#x22; | &#x22;markdown&#x22;',\n    default: '&#x22;markdown&#x22;',\n  },\n  deprecated: {\n    description: &#x22;Shows a deprecation warning when the attribute is used.&#x22;,\n    type: &#x22;boolean&#x22;,\n    default: &#x22;false&#x22;,\n  },\n  deprecationMessage: {\n    description: &#x22;Custom deprecation text.&#x22;,\n    type: &#x22;string&#x22;,\n    default: '&#x22;&#x22;',\n  },\n  default: {\n    description: &#x22;Default value used during planning when the attribute is not set.&#x22;,\n    type: &#x22;unknown&#x22;,\n    default: &#x22;undefined&#x22;,\n  },\n}\"\n/>"},"295":{"id":"/docs/concepts/schema-14","page_id":"/docs/concepts/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/schema#attributeoptions","content":"**Common patterns**"},"296":{"id":"/docs/concepts/schema-15","page_id":"/docs/concepts/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/schema#attributeoptions","content":"`optional: true, computed: true` together means \"user can set it, or the provider will compute a default\". This is useful for auto-assigned values like `name` or `region` that the user might want to control."},"297":{"id":"/docs/concepts/schema-16","page_id":"/docs/concepts/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/schema#nestedblock","content":"Represents a block that can appear zero or more times (e.g. `network_interface`, `tags`)."},"298":{"id":"/docs/concepts/schema-